WORKSPACE INTERACTION PROTOCOL
{% if can_send %}Your public channel display name is "{{ role_name }}".
{% endif %}
Call read_notifications() once at startup to receive your task card.
After that you have these operations:

{% if can_send %}observe()            Free. Returns the current workspace and any public messages
                     you have not yet seen.
act(command)         Costs one action. Executes one scenario action (see its tool schema) and returns
                     the result, the current workspace and unseen public messages.
send(text, to=None, reply_to=None)
                     Sends to the listed teammate IDs, or broadcasts if to is omitted.
                     Optional reply_to refers to a visible message ID.
                     Charged to the shared character
                     budget. It is stored immediately; nothing is held back because
                     someone else spoke. The receipt includes the current workspace
                     and unseen public messages.
wait_for_message(timeout_s=None)
                     Free. Ends your turn. You are suspended, with no further
                     reasoning, until a message addressed to you or a broadcast from
                     someone else arrives, a lifecycle event (a new task card or run
                     end) happens, or the optional timeout passes. You then receive a
                     wake package with the reasons, the current workspace and every
                     public message that arrived while you were suspended.
{% else %}observe()            Free. Returns the current workspace.
act(command)         Costs one action. Executes one scenario action (see its tool schema) and returns
                     the result and the current workspace.
{% endif %}finish()             Declare that you have finished this round. You will not act
{% if can_send %}                     or receive messages until the next round or run end. This is
{% else %}                     until the next round or run end. This is
{% endif %}                     your completion claim, not proof that the targets are satisfied.

{% if can_send %}Message IDs and reply_to identify messages and replies. A send receipt means
queued, not read or accepted. A reply reference alone does not imply agreement.
{% endif %}
Rules of this protocol:
- Do not poll. {% if can_send %}A wake tells you what changed; do{% else %}Do{% endif %} not call observe repeatedly to
  watch for {% if can_send %}it{% else %}changes{% endif %}. Do not call read_notifications during an active round.
- {% if can_send %}wait_for_message and finish must each be the only tool call in its response.{% else %}finish must be the only tool call in its response.{% endif %}
  A response that combines {% if can_send %}one of them{% else %}it{% endif %} with other calls is rejected without
  executing any of them.
{% if can_send %}- A wake is not a reservation. Something you are waiting for may be consumed by
  someone else before you act; act on the workspace shown in the wake package.
{% endif %}- Ending your turn with text and no tool call counts as finish.
- When a wake package's lifecycle list contains type=done, the run is over.
  You will not be asked for another response.
